<span class="glossary-term">Alkalinity<span class="tooltip">The capacity of water to neutralise acids — provides buffering against pH changes. Important for aquatic life and water treatment.</span></span><br>
<span class="glossary-term">TDS (Total Dissolved Solids)<span class="tooltip">The total concentration of dissolved minerals in water, measured in mg/L. Related to EC but expressed differently.</span></span><br>
<span class="glossary-term">Hypoxia<span class="tooltip">Low dissolved oxygen conditions (typically < 2 mg/L) that can cause fish kills and stress aquatic life.</span></span><br>
<span class="glossary-term">Field blank<span class="tooltip">A sample of distilled water processed in the field exactly like a real sample — used to check for contamination during collection and handling.</span></span><br>
<span class="glossary-term">Riparian zone<span class="tooltip">The vegetated area alongside waterways. Healthy riparian zones filter runoff, stabilise banks, and provide shade that moderates water temperature.</span></span>
